  "question": {
    "text": "Let <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>X</mi></math>&nbsp;be a random variable having binomial distribution <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>B</mi><mfenced><mrow><mn>7</mn><mo>,</mo><mi>p</mi></mrow></mfenced></math>. If <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>P</mi><mfenced><mrow><mi>X</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>3</mn></mrow></mfenced><mo>=</mo><mn>5</mn><mi>P</mi><mfenced><mrow><mi>X</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>4</mn></mrow></mfenced></math>, then the sum of the mean and the variance of&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>X</mi></math> is"
  },
